# How to cite this repository. The article is not published yet: until it is, the software below is the citable
# object, and a Zenodo release of a tag gives it a DOI that cannot drift the way a branch can. Once the article is
# out, add it as `preferred-citation` (the commented block at the end) so that citation managers prefer the paper and
# still credit the code.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this pipeline or its results, please cite it as below.
title: >-
  Leakage-Free Benchmarking of Classical Machine Learning and Graph Neural Networks for Low-Data TgDHFR
  Bioactivity Prediction: analysis pipeline
abstract: >-
  Reproducible pipeline that audits the data leakage of a published TgDHFR QSAR study and benchmarks classical
  stacking ensembles against graph neural networks under a leakage-free nested cross-validation protocol, with an
  applicability-domain-aware virtual screening and a generalization cohort of MoleculeACE targets. Every number the
  manuscript states is exported by the pipeline as a LaTeX macro, so the text cannot drift from the results.
